    },
    {
      "name": "person__orcid",
      "description": "ORCID identifier for the person",
      "comments": [
        "Persistent identifier for the individual; the preferred way to identify a person",
        "Example: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1885-1511"
      ],
      "from_schema": "http://w3id.org/lambda/",
      "slot_uri": "http://w3id.org/lambda/orcid",
      "alias": "orcid",
      "owner": "Person",
      "domain_of": [
        "Person"
      ],
      "range": "uriorcurie",
      "pattern": "^https://orcid\\.org/\\d{4}-\\d{4}-\\d{4}-\\d{3}[0-9X]$",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "person__full_name",
      "description": "Full formal name of the person, as they write it in publications",
      "comments": [
        "Overlaps the inherited `title`, deliberately but not redundantly. `title` is the display label every NamedThing carries and is what a listing shows (\"Clyde Smith\"); `full_name` is the formal name a citation needs (\"Clyde A. Smith\"). They are equal often enough that a consumer reading only one is usually fine, so record `title` whenever `full_name` is known - a Person with a formal name and no display label is awkward for every UI that treats NamedThing uniformly.",
        "Where the two would be identical, carrying only `title` is correct and `full_name` adds nothing."
      ],
      "from_schema": "http://w3id.org/lambda/",
      "close_mappings": [
        "http://w3id.org/lambda/title"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "http://w3id.org/lambda/full_name",
      "alias": "full_name",
      "owner": "Person",
      "domain_of": [
        "Person"
      ],
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "person__given_name",
      "description": "Given (personal) name, where the name has been parsed into parts",
      "from_schema": "http://w3id.org/lambda/",
      "slot_uri": "http://w3id.org/lambda/given_name",
      "alias": "given_name",
      "owner": "Person",
      "domain_of": [
        "Person"
      ],
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "person__family_name",
      "description": "Family name, where the name has been parsed into parts",
      "from_schema": "http://w3id.org/lambda/",
      "slot_uri": "http://w3id.org/lambda/family_name",
      "alias": "family_name",
      "owner": "Person",
      "domain_of": [
        "Person"
      ],
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
